<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Humban</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Humban was one of the chief gods of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, worshipped from the 3rd millennium BCE. He was regarded as a lord of the sky and closely linked with kingship, and his name formed part of many royal names, such as Humban-nikash and Humban-haltash. Some scholars identify him with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napirisha">Napirisha</a>, 'the great god', worshipped at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chogha-zanbil">Chogha Zanbil</a>.</p></div>
